<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Supreme Soviet of the Estonian SSR</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1940">1940</a>–<a href="/years/1992">1992</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Supreme Council of the Republic of Estonia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Supreme Soviet of the Estonian SSR was the legislature of Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a>. On 16 November 1988 it declared Estonia's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> and the supremacy of its laws over those of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>. Elected freely in 1990 and renamed the Supreme Council, it declared the restoration of full independence on 20 August 1991, during the failed coup in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/supreme-soviet-of-the-estonian-ssr.jpg" alt="Supreme Soviet of the Estonian SSR" width="320" height="354" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jam123 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblem_of_the_Estonian_SSR.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
